# nativetap — mobile design rules for AI agents (Cursor variant)

You are building MOBILE UI. Before writing or reviewing any phone-screen
interface, consult the nativetap data:

- Rulebook: .claude/skills/nativetap/references/thumb-rules.md (the 40 thumb rules, P0-P5)
- Searchable data: .claude/skills/nativetap/data/*.csv — 42 domains, 461 rows
  (run: python3 .claude/skills/nativetap/scripts/search.py "<topic>")

Hard rules that are non-negotiable (P0):
- Touch targets >= 44x44pt iOS / 48x48dp Android, 8px+ apart
- Contrast >= 4.5:1 body text, verified in BOTH light and dark mode
- Layout survives 200% font scale
- iOS gets HIG conventions; Android gets Material 3. Never average them.
- Every icon-only button has an accessibility label

Search before you design. Cite the row you applied in code comments.
